# The load and churn harness, natively, for the machine it is built on:
# scenario G (a reliable-UDP game server), S (HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and
# WebSocket under connection churn, half over TLS) and I (idle WebSockets
# at scale). See tests/load/LoadMain.hx, and the README's Testing section
# for how to run each.
#
#   haxe ci/load.hxml
#   ./export/load/LoadMain game --clients 1000 --hz 60 --seconds 600
#
# CI does not run this: like ci/soak.hxml it is a long measurement, not a
# gate. For the crossbyte-libuv backend, add its defines (README).
-cp src
-cp tests/load
-D HXCPP_M64
-main LoadMain
--cpp export/load
--macro crossbyte._internal.macro.HostPlatform.define()
--macro crossbyte._internal.macro.StdOverrides.use()
